# BusinessProfiles

**Status:** Draft — founder review required
**Phase:** 5 — Application System

## Purpose

Holds the structured profile(s) `EligibilityEngine.md`,
`MatchingAlgorithm.md`, and `GrantWriter-Agent` all reference. This is the
single source of truth for "who is applying" — every other file references
it rather than restating business facts inline.

## Profile Schema

```
- Business name:
- Entity type: (sole proprietorship, LLC, S-corp, etc.)
- Industry/trade classification:
- Location(s) served:
- Years in operation:
- Employee count:
- Annual revenue range: (range, not exact figure — used for size-standard
  eligibility checks, not for narrative)
- Certifications held: (e.g. minority/veteran/woman-owned, if applicable
  and if the business holds them — never assumed)
- Prior grant history: (awarded / applied-not-awarded / none)
- Key qualifications/differentiators: (for narrative use)
```

## Notes

- This file should be filled in directly by the founder, not inferred or
  guessed at by any agent — profile accuracy is foundational to every
  eligibility and scoring decision downstream, so fabricated or assumed
  fields here would propagate errors through the entire system
- If BAE intends to run grants for more than one business (e.g. BHI plus
  other portfolio companies), this file should hold one profile block per
  business, each independently referenced by opportunity records

